; t28_anonfn.n — v16 anonymous functions: `:` defines an inline fn cell,
; `':` applies one immediately against the list below (spread as args).
; The closing `ret` is load-bearing and must sit on the same line.
; Run: nk comp/tests/t28_anonfn.n

; 1. anon callback at a consumer (adjacent -> inlined)
[1 2 3] xs!
xs : 2 mul ret array_map dup!
dup to_json "[2,4,6]" eq check
xs : 2 gt ret filter to_json "[3]" eq check

; 2. binds inside an anon body (vars reload, so reuse needs no dup)
xs : x! x x mul ret array_map to_json "[1,4,9]" eq check

; 3. while with two anon bodies sharing the caller's frame
0 i2!
3 : i2 3 lt ret : i2 1 add i2! ret while
i2 3 eq check

; 4. try / spawn with anon bodies
: 1 0 div ret try ok# _#
ok 0 eq check
: 42 ret spawn ch!
ch dequeue 42 eq check

; 5. ': apply — list is the arg vector, spread onto the stack
[3 4] ': add ret 7 eq check
[5] ': 2 mul ret 10 eq check
[3 4] ': a! b! a b add ret 7 eq check

; 6. the value form stores like any fn cell; apply works on it
: x! x x mul ret sqf!
[7] sqf apply 49 eq check
sqf type_of 22 eq check

; 7. a nested anon callback inside an apply body
[[1 2 3]] ': l! l : 2 mul ret array_map ret to_json "[2,4,6]" eq check

; 8. named labels still work alongside anons
xs pred filter to_json "[3]" eq check
ret
pred: v!
  ret v 2 gt
